### Stage 4 demo (B4.10). Run the dev server (`npm run dev`), `npm run migrate:deploy`, seed the dev accounts (`npm run seed:dev`),
### start the job worker in another terminal (`npm run jobs:worker`), then sign in as each dev account and send these with that session cookie.
### The same walk-through runs automatically in tests/stage4ExitGate.test.ts.

@base = http://localhost:3000
@org = figbloom

### 1. As Management: settings overview, then rotate the website key; the old key keeps working for 6 hours
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/settings/overview

###
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/integrations/website-key
Content-Type: application/json

{ "graceHours": 6 }

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/integrations/website-key/rejected

###
PUT {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/integrations/whatsapp
Content-Type: application/json

{ "number": "0700 123 456", "defaultMessage": "Hello {{name}}, this is Figbloom." }

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/integrations

### 2. Automations: switch the follow-up task off, then see what the rules did
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/automations

###
PATCH {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/automations/NEW_LEAD_FOLLOW_UP_TASK
Content-Type: application/json

{ "enabled": false }

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/automations/runs

### 3. Reference data: a value in use can be hidden, not deleted
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/reference-admin/services

###
DELETE {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/reference-admin/services/<serviceId>

###
PATCH {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/reference-admin/services/<serviceId>
Content-Type: application/json

{ "hidden": true }

### 4. Data migration with a bad row: create, upload, map, validate, dry run, import, review, roll back
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "entity": "COMPANY" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions/<sessionId>/file?fileName=companies.csv
Content-Type: text/csv

name,email
Gate One,one@x.test
Gate Bad,nope
Gate Two,two@x.test

###
PUT {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions/<sessionId>/mapping
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mapping": { "name": "name", "email": "email" } }

###
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions/<sessionId>/validate

###
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions/<sessionId>/dry-run

###
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions/<sessionId>/import
Content-Type: application/json

{ "confirm": true }

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions/<sessionId>

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions/<sessionId>/errors

###
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/data-migration/sessions/<sessionId>/rollback

### 5. Data and privacy: file an erasure; two different Management members confirm
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/privacy/requests
Content-Type: application/json

{ "kind": "ERASURE", "contactId": "<contactId>", "evidenceNotes": "Requester verified by email and ID" }

###
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/privacy/requests/<requestId>/confirm-erasure

### (sign in as a second Management member)
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/privacy/requests/<requestId>/confirm-erasure

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/privacy

### 6. As Sales: capture a lead, then replay an offline batch twice
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/quick-capture
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-capture-0001

{ "name": "Amina Odhiambo", "phone": "0722 123 456", "note": "Met at the expo", "followUp": { "title": "Send the quote" } }

###
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/sync/batch
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mutations": [
  { "clientId": "demo-sync-capture-0001", "kind": "QUICK_CAPTURE", "payload": { "name": "Offline Person", "phone": "0712 345 678" } },
  { "clientId": "demo-sync-task-0001", "kind": "TASK_CREATE", "payload": { "title": "Offline task", "leadId": "ref:demo-sync-capture-0001" } }
] }

### Send the same batch again: every item answers DUPLICATE and nothing new is created
POST {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/sync/batch
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mutations": [
  { "clientId": "demo-sync-capture-0001", "kind": "QUICK_CAPTURE", "payload": { "name": "Offline Person", "phone": "0712 345 678" } },
  { "clientId": "demo-sync-task-0001", "kind": "TASK_CREATE", "payload": { "title": "Offline task", "leadId": "ref:demo-sync-capture-0001" } }
] }

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/sync/status

### 7. Push and the installable app
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/push/config

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/pwa/manifest

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/pwa/version

### 8. As Management: the audit log shows all of it, filtered, and as CSV
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/audit/events?action=data_migration.*&dateFrom=2026-10-01

###
GET {{base}}/api/orgs/{{org}}/audit/events/export?entityType=ImportSession
